WEBVTT

NOTE
Automatic English captions. Generated locally and checked with additional audio decodes; not fully audited by listening.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.460
Most of what your workflows produce is
structured data. Statuses, scores, results

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:10.240
you want to keep and act on later. That's
what tables are for. They're like a

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:14.720
database built right into your workspace
with rows and columns your workflows can

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:20.080
read from and write back to, run after
run. Anything you want to track, process

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:25.380
in batches, or build on over time should
live in a table. Let me show you how they

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:30.300
work. Every business runs on small facts
like this one, a company name someone

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:31.300
wrote down.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:37.480
In a table, that fact lives inside a row,
one record that keeps everything about

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:39.000
this lead in one place.

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:45.140
Each column gives its values, a type,
text, numbers, dates, so every record

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:46.800
keeps the same reliable shape.

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:54.400
Zoom out, and this is a table, typed
columns over rows, where each row is one

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:55.400
real record.

00:00:57.220 --> 00:01:01.320
New leads keep arriving, and each one
lands as another clean row.

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:09.140
And the shape can grow. A new column
starts from a type, text, number, boolean,

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:14.840
date, or JSON, and a column can even be
filled by a workflow. Pick boolean, and a

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:18.520
qualified column lands with a real
checkbox on every record, matching the

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:19.520
status beside it.

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:26.340
The table stays current as work happens.
The moment a deal moves, its status moves

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:27.340
with it.

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:32.900
And the same shape works for anything you
track, support tickets, orders, any

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:34.680
structured record your team keeps.

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:41.960
A table is a home for your records,
alongside the workflows that will put them

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:42.960
to work.
